course: dictionary
lesson: 1748
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. Classic can be a noun: a classic is a book, film, song or other work that is very good and has been admired by people for a long time. As an adjective, classic means very typical, a perfect example of its kind. «Mistakes were made» is the classic example, so here it means the best, most typical example.
explain: Check the clues around the word. In «That's classic!» said after a silly moment, classic means very typical or very funny. Ask: what would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Classic can also mean simple and stylish in a way that does not go out of fashion, like a classic car. Classics, with a capital C, is the study of ancient Greek and Roman languages and culture. When context is not enough, a dictionary settles it.
fact: Classic can be a noun (a classic) or an adjective (classic).
fact: A classic is a book, film, song or other work that is very good and has been admired for a long time.
fact: «A classic mistake» means a typical mistake, one that many people make.
fact: «The classic example» means the perfect example of its kind.
fact: Classics, with a capital C, is the study of ancient Greek and Roman languages and culture.
exercise: «Mistakes were made» is the classic example: it admits something went wrong but never says who made the mistakes. What does classic mean here? | A new fashion that everyone is wearing | A very old castle | *The perfect, typical example of its kind | A sad story
exercise: Mia says, «Let's read a children's classic tonight.» What is a children's classic? | A party game for children | A bedtime routine for children | A short, rude comment | *A children's book that is very good and has been admired for a long time
exercise: The dictionary says «gōngxǐ fācái» means «wishing you wealth and luck!», the classic New Year wish to grown-ups. What does «gōngxǐ fācái» mean? | Goodbye until next year | Happy birthday to you | *Wishing you wealth and luck! | Sorry for being late
test: Tracing catches the classic traps: a line after a loop runs once, not every time. In this sentence, what does classic mean? | A trap that is made of wood | A very old trap from long ago | *Typical and well known, the usual trap to watch for | A funny trap that makes people laugh
test: Ben says, «My dad's old car is a classic.» What does Ben suggest? | It is a bicycle with two wheels | *It is an older car that people admire and that does not go out of fashion | It is broken and must be thrown away | It is a bus for school
exam: «Leaving out "e", the commonest letter in English, is the hardest classic challenge.» What does classic mean here? | A challenge that is played with a ball | A quick, easy game for a rainy day | A challenge for very old people | *A typical, well-known challenge of its kind
